> 
> I'm wearing speedboots if that matters (didn't think to wait on the hole  
> just incase I'd fall on the next turn, if indeed the owlbear's death  
> happened between turns or something - I vaguely remember higher speed  
> being funny on some things).
> 
> Is this a bug (I searched the two bug files for 'dig', 'speed', and  
> 'hole' without finding this), or just some common oddity with speed  
> boots?

Not dropping afterwards isn't a bug. There is room to stand at a hole 
location so if you didn't drop in the first place then you are ok. Don't 
know if you can use > to drop, but you cannot use it to go into a pit.

If you don't know there is a possibility to escape a hole and if you do 
you are left standing in the hole location. I know that this works with 
(spiked)pits also, but I don't know if it work with trapdoors and I'm 
now too lazy and drunk to check the sources.

IMHO there should be a chance that you and the grapper both fall down 
and a chance that you fall on the grapper which might both cushion the 
fall and make it to release you. If on the other hand the grapper falls 
on you it should make considerable damage.

